today i want to take a few minutes to  tell you about a really innovative  platform doing some very cool things in  the world of decentralized finance defy  and the project is called la cucina  we've partnered with la cucina to create  this video essentially what la cucina is  doing is incentivizing defy users to  discover great defy projects which  otherwise might get overlooked by  rewarding users with extra benefits when  providing liquidity without the user  needing to stake the foundation of la  cucina  is and really what they're setting out  to do  is remove the inequities that we often  see in d5 because la cucina believes  everyone should have the same ability to  reap the rewards of their crypto but la  cucina applies this egalitarian  philosophy to d5 projects as well  there's too many barriers for people  trying to set up  a farm on a major decks  your project already has to be huge for  you to see success so a lot of smaller  but well deserving projects get ignored  and lost in the mix  la cucina's solution to this problem  is to create a community oriented defy  platform that stimulates engagement  between projects and users and la cucina  drives this by offering rewards for user  engagement which in turn grows a  project's community we wouldn't call la  cucina  a defy exchange per se  in contrast la cucina works with  exchanges to complement them it's an  engaged community where d5 users who  want to find great projects actually can  and users can judge projects by their  merit instead of by their size so la  cucina puts these projects in a much  better position to compete with bigger  projects but how does it work let's talk  about one of the central innovations  that la cucina is bringing to the table  called external farming which la cucina  uses to promote emerging defy projects  on the platform la cucina monitors and  supports a long list of d5 projects and  they're always adding more to the list  if you're someone providing liquidity to  liquidity pools for one of these  projects on a major decks outside of la  cucina  blacina's external farming lets you get  even more benefits on top of the swap  fees you've already been earning you can  farm earnings without having to stake  anything or move your stakings another  really important concept in la cucina  are what they call ovens and now we're  getting to why it's called la cucina  which of course means the kitchen an  oven is similar to a crypto farm which a  lot of us are familiar with an oven lets  you get extra perks without having to  stake and with tons of flexibility and  every oven in la cucina every oven in  the kitchen  represents a liquidity pool and each one  has what they call cooking plans each  cooking plan is a reward policy being  used to promote different parts of  liquidity provisioning like the timing  or the duration or the amount so cooking  plans are what determine the allocation  of the rewards among liquidity providers  every cooking plan is just a  mathematical function which i won't get  into but it's interesting to read about  the math behind it on la cucina's medium  page on  in an article that explains how it all  works nfts are also a major component of  la cucina you can collect buy and sell  nfts on the platform you can actually  cook the nfts in the kitchen too a lot  of people complain that nfts don't do  anything nfts on la cucina are not just  things to look at although you know the  art may well be great but each type of  nft on la cucina has a utility on the  platform and there's a few different  types of nfts they serve different  purposes secret ingredients dishes  italians talions are the tradable  customizable sort of like someone's  avatar inside la cucina and when you  cook the secret ingredients together  you'll get a new nft  the reward boosting dish the dishes have  a multiplier from 1.1 x to 10x  and they can be activated in any oven to  increase your share of rewards in that  oven all of the nfts kind of fit 